# One reviewed false positive per line, as: path:rule-id:line
#
# CI flagged a fake secret in your PR? Read the three values off the finding
# box in the failed CI log and add the line here, then push:
#
#   ┌─private-key──○                    -> rule-id
#   │ 12 │ const key = "REDACTED"       -> line
#   │   path ...... path/to/file.go     -> path
#   => path/to/file.go:private-key:12
#
# Even simpler when you can edit the line: put `betterleaks:allow` on it instead.
# Add a short comment above each entry saying why it is a false positive.

# Sample RSA keypair shipped in Nhost demo/tutorial .secrets.example templates
# (intentionally public; copied to a real .secrets by the user).
examples/demos/backend-cats/.secrets.example:private-key:10
examples/tutorials/backend-notes/.secrets.example:private-key:10
